# Client protocol

The server sends events over the socket as {type, payload}.

| type | payload |
|---|---|
| message | id, userId, text, sentAt |
| message.deleted | id |
| typing | userId |
| presence | userId, status |

Android clients older than 5.2 (about 30 percent of installs) decode message payloads with a strict
schema and crash on any field they don't know. Every client ignores event types it doesn't know.
